From 28d38500bf7ba17e8c3ade38162130162f40fc0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksa Sarai <asarai@suse.de>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:43:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] tty: add TIOCGPTPEER ioctl

When opening the slave end of a PTY, it is currently necessary for
userspace to derive the slave's pathname (/dev/pts/N) from the master
fd, open it and hope that it refers to the same PTY. Inside a mount
namespace that does not share the devpts instance with the one the
master was taken from, or when /dev/pts is not mounted at all, this
is not possible, and even where it is possible it is a race against
the PTY being closed and the number reused.

This adds the TIOCGPTPEER ioctl, which opens the slave end of the PTY
the master fd refers to and returns an fd to it, with the open flags
given as the argument.

This is the final v4.13 form of the feature, squashed from three
mainline commits:

  54ebbfb16034 "tty: add TIOCGPTPEER ioctl" (Aleksa Sarai)
  c6325179238f "tty: Fix TIOCGPTPEER ioctl definition" (Gleb Fotengauer-Malinovskiy)
  311fc65c9fb9 "pty: Repair TIOCGPTPEER" (Eric W. Biederman)

The first two together define TIOCGPTPEER as _IO('T', 0x41)
(0x5441) in the generic and per-architecture ioctls headers. The third
replaced the cached struct path in tty->link->driver_data, which leaked
and could point into the wrong devpts instance, with ptm_open_peer():
it recomputes the slave's path from the ptmx file at ioctl time through
the new devpts_mntget(), and the ioctl is handled in tty_ioctl() because
it needs the struct file.

Backport to 4.9: the 4.9 tty_ioctl() switch has no default case (that
came with tty_jobctrl.c in v4.12), so the new case sits after
TIOCSSERIAL at the end of the switch. ptm_open_peer() lives next to
ptmx_cdev under CONFIG_UNIX98_PTYS as in mainline; the pty_close(),
ptmx_open() and pty_unix98_ioctl() changes of the first commit are
reverted by the third and are not included. The TIOCGPTPEER define
sits after TIOCVHANGUP rather than after TIOCGEXCL so the hunk does not
depend on what a vendor tree appends after TIOCGEXCL (Samsung adds
TIOCPMGET and friends there).

systemd 258 removed its fallback for kernels without this ioctl (commit
1d522f1a8); run0, systemd-run -t, machinectl shell and nspawn consoles
fail without it. It is not needed to boot.
